<newsitem itemid="366509" id="root" date="1997-02-10" xml:lang="en">
<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Interleisure half year share rises.</title>
<headline>Interleisure half year share rises.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended Dec 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Pre-excep shr, attrib (cts)     15.1   vs 13.0</p>
<p>    Post-excep shr, attrib (cts)    25.5   vs 12.4</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 6.75	  vs  6.00</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   48.44	 vs  23.51</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   60.38	 vs  35.52</p>
<p>    Tax			 11.97	 vs  11.80</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   0.90 gain   vs  0.81 paid</p>
<p>    Turnover		  250.37	vs  226.75</p>
<p>    Exceptional items     18.13 gain  vs 1.07 loss</p>
<p>Div payable: March 17</p>
<p>On register: February 21</p>
<p>Full name: Interleisure Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - South Africa's Interleisure Ltd said a good line-up at its Ster-Kinekor cinema chain would enhance trading in the second half. But it added a decline in turnover elsewhere in the group would temper this advance.</p>
<p>&quot;Earnings growth for the year is expected to be in line with that achieved for the first six months,&quot; the firm said.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
